<%# THE MONEY ROW — Home's first two answers as three stat tiles (two-shapes spec §3).
    Local: `presenter` (HomePresenter). It replaces `home/_hero.html.erb`.

    ** WHAT MOVED AND WHAT DID NOT. ** The THREE FIGURES and the negative arms' SENTENCES are §2's,
    unchanged and pinned by the examples `hero_spec.rb` carried into `money_spec.rb`: in checking,
    free = pot − Σ claims, the claimed figure, and the overdraft line. What changed is the SHAPE.

    ** THE TILES ARE SIBLINGS NOW, NOT A CARD OF CARDS (2026-09-06 layout ruling). ** This partial
    used to render one bordered, padded card whose three children were themselves bordered, padded
    cards: two borders and two paddings around every figure, and at 375px a third of the first screen
    was padding. The tiles are the cards, `index.html.erb` owns the grid that lays them out, and the
    money region's hook (`[data-money]`) rides on that grid — so nothing on this screen is drawn
    inside a box whose only job is to hold boxes.

    ** THE ORDER IS THE ANSWER FIRST. ** Free to spend leads, because it is the figure the user came
    for and the only one their bank cannot tell them; in checking and what sits outside it are the
    two facts it is derived from. The free tile SPANS the row and the other two halve the line
    beneath it, at every width up to `lg`, where all three stand side by side.

    ** THE BAR IS THE SUBLINE AS A PICTURE. ** Two segments of the pot, free and claimed, off ONE
    figure (`#claimed_percent`) so they cannot add up to something that is not the whole. It is drawn
    on the free tile because free is the number it explains.

    THE WORDS ARE THE USER'S (answers-first §3): in checking, free, claimed, other accounts. "Set
    aside", "spoken for", "available", "goal" and "fund" are not on this screen — nothing is moved
    anywhere and nothing holds money; a rule CLAIMS money where it sits. %>

<%# TILE 1 — THE ONE DERIVED NUMBER: `pot − Σ claims` (§2). The sage tile, because it is the answer
    the user came for. Never clamped: a negative free renders negative, in red (§4 — it is a signal,
    not a refusal). It spans the row below `lg`, so it is full width on a phone — which is what
    "emphasised" means at a width that has no room for emphasis of any other kind. %>
<div class="bg-brand-light border border-brand rounded p-4 lg:p-5 col-span-full lg:col-span-1" data-tile="free">
  <p class="text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-wide text-brand-dark">Free to spend</p>
  <p class="mt-1 text-3xl font-semibold tabular-nums <%= presenter.free_to_spend.negative? ? "text-status-danger" : "text-brand-dark" %>"
     data-free>
    <%= number_to_currency(presenter.free_to_spend) %>
  </p>

  <%# THE BAR AND THE ONE LINE THAT EXPLAINS IT, ON ONE ROW WHERE THERE IS ROOM. `flex-wrap` rather
      than a breakpoint: the sentence drops under the bar exactly when it stops fitting beside it,
      which is a different width on the free tile's three shapes (full row at `sm`, a third at `lg`)
      than any single breakpoint could name.

      THE TWO SEGMENTS are drawn only where the pot is a quantity to be a fraction of — an empty or
      overdrawn account is not, and a bar there would have to invent a denominator
      (`#claimed_percent` is nil, and this renders nothing).

      THE CLAIMED SEGMENT CARRIES THE HOOK AND THE WIDTH, deliberately: at 0% a fill has no width and
      Capybara does not consider it visible, so the percent rides on the track — `_this_period`'s own
      rule, and the app's other bars draw the same way. %>
  <div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-3 gap-y-2">
    <% if claimed = presenter.claimed_percent %>
      <div class="h-2 min-w-24 flex-1 bg-white rounded-full overflow-hidden"
           role="progressbar"
           aria-valuenow="<%= claimed %>"
           aria-valuemin="0"
           aria-valuemax="100"
           aria-label="<%= number_to_currency(presenter.total_claims) %> of checking claimed by your rules"
           data-claimed-bar="<%= claimed %>">
        <div class="h-2 <%= presenter.short? ? "bg-status-danger" : "bg-brand-darker" %>"
             style="width: <%= claimed %>%;"
             data-claimed-fill></div>
      </div>
    <% end %>

    <%# ** THE SUBLINE, AND ITS POSITIVE ARM IS NOW ONE SHORT CLAUSE (2026-09-06 layout ruling). **
        It read "$X of checking is claimed by your rules, and $Y sits in N other accounts" — a
        two-fact sentence three lines deep on a phone, whose second fact is the third tile's whole
        subject: the figure AND the account names, said once, beside it. So the parked-elsewhere
        clause is gone from here and the tile is where "how much sits elsewhere" is answered. What
        stays is the claim, which is the bar's own caption.

        ** THE NEGATIVE ARMS STAY HERE WHOLE (§2), because they are this tile's red state and there
        is no other tile they could be about. ** Each half is gated on the predicate that
        ESTABLISHES it rather than inferred from the signs of two figures:

          claimed, money elsewhere   → "Your rules claim $X more…" + "Move some in…"
          claimed, one account       → "Your rules claim $X more…" + "You have spent past what you had."
          nothing claimed, elsewhere → "Move some in…"   (the pot is under; the money exists)
          nothing claimed, one acct  → "You have spent past what you had."

        THE SECOND CLAUSE IS ABOUT PARKED MONEY AND NOTHING ELSE (fix wave — LOW-1): it was gated
        `elsif !anything_claimed?`, which made "You have spent past what you had" unreachable for the
        user it is truest of — free below zero, rules claiming, and no other account to move anything
        in from. §2 draws the line where the MONEY is, so the else takes the spec's clause.
        `_shortfall.html.erb`'s HEADLINE still splits on `#anything_claimed?`, which is a different
        question (whose fault the gap is), and that split stays. %>
    <p class="text-sm <%= presenter.free_to_spend.negative? ? "text-status-danger" : "text-brand-dark" %>"
       data-free-subline>
      <% if presenter.free_to_spend.negative? %>
        <% if presenter.anything_claimed? %>
          Your rules claim <%= number_to_currency(presenter.shortfall) %> more than checking holds.
        <% end %>
        <% if presenter.money_parked_elsewhere? %>
          Move some in from your other accounts.
        <% else %>
          You have spent past what you had.
        <% end %>
      <% else %>
        <%= number_to_currency(presenter.total_claims) %> claimed by your rules
      <% end %>
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<%# TILE 2 — THE NUMBER THE BANK APP SHOWS. `#in_checking` is `AccountLedger#pot`: main's balance,
    not the user's money everywhere, because that is the figure they can check against their phone.
    RED BELOW ZERO — a physical overdraft is money that has already gone, which no purpose-side
    figure on this screen can say.

    ONE STEP SMALLER BELOW `sm`, on this tile and the next: they are HALVES of the row there, and a
    six-figure balance at `text-2xl` is wider than 163px of tile — measured, on the account holding
    $222,544.87. The free tile keeps its `text-3xl` because it keeps the whole row. %>
<div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded p-4 lg:p-5" data-tile="checking">
  <p class="text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-500">In checking</p>
  <p class="mt-1 text-xl sm:text-2xl font-semibold tabular-nums <%= presenter.in_checking.negative? ? "text-status-danger" : "text-gray-900" %>"
     data-in-checking>
    <%= number_to_currency(presenter.in_checking) %>
  </p>
  <%# THE FACT ALONE, AND NO CONSEQUENCE (fix round 1 — MED-1). This ended "— nothing is free until
      money comes in", which is a lie for the user whose money is simply in the wrong account. Which
      of the two negative-pot states it is belongs to the free tile's subline, which is the one place
      on this row that knows. The tile is otherwise a label and a figure and nothing else. %>
  <% if presenter.in_checking.negative? %>
    <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-status-danger" data-checking-overdrawn>
      Your checking account is already spent past zero.
    </p>
  <% end %>
</div>

<%# TILE 3 — MONEY THAT IS NOT IN CHECKING (§2): shown, never subtracted from or added to anything.
    It is the fact that closes the shortfall arm's instruction, and the chips say WHICH accounts hold
    it — the one place on Home that answers "where", now that the free tile's subline no longer tries
    to and the accounts line at the foot has gone back to being a door.

    ONE ROW OF CHIPS AND NO MORE. Three names, then "+N more": a tile that wrapped a dozen account
    names would be taller than the two figures beside it and would break the row's own line.

    ABSENT WHERE THERE IS NOTHING TO SAY. `#other_accounts` empty is a user with one account, and a
    tile reading "$0.00 in 0 other accounts" would be the app inventing an absence — the same refusal
    `_accounts_line` makes about its own summary. The row becomes two tiles, and `index.html.erb`
    drops to two columns at `lg` so the pair fills it. %>
<% if presenter.other_accounts.any? %>
  <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded p-4 lg:p-5" data-tile="elsewhere" data-other-accounts>
    <%# TWO SPELLINGS OF ONE LABEL, and the short one is not a shortening for its own sake: this tile
        is half of 375px on a phone, where "In 3 other accounts" wraps to two lines and pushes the
        figure below the fold of its own tile. "Elsewhere" is the word the row is already about — the
        free tile no longer says it, the count is the accounts line's — and from `sm` the tile has
        the width to name it in full. %>
    <p class="text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-500">
      <span class="sm:hidden">Elsewhere</span>
      <span class="hidden sm:inline">In <%= pluralize(presenter.other_accounts.count, "other account") %></span>
    </p>
    <p class="mt-1 text-xl sm:text-2xl font-semibold tabular-nums text-gray-900" data-other-accounts-total>
      <%= number_to_currency(presenter.other_accounts_total) %>
    </p>
    <%# THE CHIPS ARE A WIDE-SCREEN ANSWER, and below `sm` there is no width to answer in: three
        names in half of 375px is three ellipses. The figure is the tile's job at that width, and the
        accounts line at the foot of the page is still the door to the names. %>
    <ul class="mt-2 hidden gap-1.5 overflow-hidden sm:flex">
      <% presenter.other_accounts.first(3).each do |account| %>
        <li class="min-w-0 truncate rounded bg-gray-100 px-2 py-0.5 text-xs text-gray-700"
            data-account-chip="<%= account.name %>">
          <%= account.name %>
        </li>
      <% end %>
      <% if (rest = presenter.other_accounts.count - 3).positive? %>
        <li class="shrink-0 rounded px-2 py-0.5 text-xs text-gray-500" data-more-accounts>+<%= rest %> more</li>
      <% end %>
    </ul>
  </div>
<% end %>
